Implement user story AMSD-1820: [Mozio] - The Promo code amount is NOT displayed as expected for Return trip tickets in the Mozio email confirmation

## Story Description
[Mozio] - The Promo code amount is NOT displayed as expected for Return trip tickets in the Mozio email confirmation

## Acceptance Criteria
- Given a customer purchases a return trip ticket with a promo code applied, when the Mozio confirmation email is generated, then the promo code discount amount is displayed for both the outbound and return trip segments in the email body.
- Given a return trip ticket with a promo code applied, when the confirmation email is rendered, then the promo code discount line for the return trip appears in the same format, currency, and position as the outbound trip discount line.
- Given a return trip ticket with no promo code applied, when the confirmation email is generated, then no promo code discount line is displayed for either the outbound or return trip segment.
- Given a return trip ticket where the promo code discount is zero, when the confirmation email is generated, then no discount line is rendered for either segment and no zero-value or placeholder discount row appears.
- Given a return trip ticket where the promo code fully offsets one leg, when the confirmation email is generated, then each leg displays a non-negative discount amount, no discount entry is missing for either leg, and the sum of the per-leg discount amounts equals the total promo code discount applied to the order.
- Given the sample order payload for Order ID 25519 (reference 20260225-94VW5CLD), when the confirmation email is generated, then the return trip promo code discount amount is present and matches the expected value from the order data.
- Given a one-way trip ticket with a promo code applied, when the Mozio confirmation email is generated, then the promo code discount amount is displayed for the single trip segment exactly as before the return-trip fix was applied.
- Given a return trip ticket where the promo code discount data for the return leg is null or missing in the order payload, when the confirmation email is generated, then the email is produced without error and the outbound segment discount is still displayed correctly.





